-- title:
--   Twice the width of a moduli place counts level-preserving automorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field, let $q'$ be a prime with $\kappa$ of characteristic $q'$ and $q'\ge 5$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q'\nmid M'$. Let $W$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ and let $C$ be an additive subgroup of the group of points of its affine model which is additively cyclic with $\operatorname{card} C = M'$. Let $P$ be a place of the $\kappa$-subfield $\kappa(j(q),\,j(q^{M'}))$ of the Laurent series field generated by `jqModC` and its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion, i.e. a valuation subring of that field containing $\kappa$, distinct from the whole field and a principal ideal ring. Assume that the valuation subring of $P$ is the preimage, under the inclusion of $\kappa(j(q),j(q^{M'}))$ into the full modular function field, of the valuation subring of `moduliPlace κ M' W C`, the place attached to the moduli point of the pair $(W,g)$ for a point $g$ of order $M'$ with $C$ its multiples (the defining case distinction falling back on the place at $q=\infty$ when no such $g$ exists). Then twice $\operatorname{placeWidth}_{M'}(P)$, which is the natural-number quotient of `jWidth` of the residue of $j(q)$ at $P$ (namely $3$ if that residue is $0$, $2$ if it is $1728$, and $1$ otherwise) by `placeRamificationJ M' P`, equals the number of additive endomorphisms $\iota$ of the points of $W$ that lie in `rationalHomSet κ W W` (that is, are zero or rationally represented), admit a two-sided inverse $\iota'$ again in `rationalHomSet κ W W`, and satisfy $\iota(C)=C$.
--
--   This is the local form of the classical count of the fibres of $X_0(M')\to X(1)$: the ramification index of a moduli place over the $j$-line is the index of the subgroup of automorphisms of $W$ preserving $C$ inside the full automorphism group of $W$, whose order is twice the width at $j(W)$ in characteristic at least $5$. It is used in the computation of Hecke matrices on the special fibre at level $M'$ and in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison of place widths with class weights, and has a further variant stated in terms of the characteristic.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_two_mul_placeWidth_eq_natCard_rationalAut_map_eq_of_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace.lean

